Planning

While many already will have, everyone on the interview schedule should formally review the candidate-submitted material per [rfd147]. Before the interview, the Oxide employee should further read all of the narrative reviews of a candidate: it is expected that these narratives will contain questions that a reviewer might have had based on the materials. In many cases, there aren’t many open questions with a candidate <span style="color: #db89c8;">(candidates that have many open questions tend to be disqualified earlier in the materials evaluation process)</span>, but in some cases, the open questions may be significant enoughto merit a pre-meeting to discuss or coordinate approach. These pre-meetings should seek to understand what the team wishes to better understand over the course of conversations — and who will do what.